FL,346,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34502
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F345A1786555124
OL,3,CDrought conditions exposes remains of
OL,4,Cvillage underneath Rutland Water
OL,6,FResidents in the hamlet, along with
OL,7,Fother small villages including Middle
OL,8,FHambleton, were relocated to other
OL,9,Fareas before the buildings were
OL,10,Fdemolished and the area flooded in the
OL,11,F1970s to create the reservoir.
OL,13,FIt comes as the East Midlands became
OL,14,Fthe latest region to move into drought
OL,15,Fstatus on Monday, along with
OL,16,FNorthamptonshire amongst other areas.
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G2/7
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,346,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34503
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F345A1786555124
OL,3,CDrought conditions exposes remains of
OL,4,Cvillage underneath Rutland Water
OL,6,FThe creation of the reservoir, which
OL,7,Finvolved damming the Gwash valley near
OL,8,FEmpingham, was finished in 1976 and
OL,9,Fflooding took a further three years,
OL,10,FLeicestershire and Rutland Wildlife
OL,11,FTrust said.
OL,13,FMore than 3,000 acres of land were
OL,14,Fsubmerged to create one of the largest
OL,15,Fman-made bodies of water in western
OL,16,FEurope, covering more than four square
OL,17,Fmiles, with cottages, farms and
OL,18,Ffarmhouses destroyed to make way for
OL,19,Fit.
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G3/7
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,346,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34504
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F345A1786555124
OL,3,CDrought conditions exposes remains of
OL,4,Cvillage underneath Rutland Water
OL,6,FAt its maximum, the reservoir is 34
OL,7,Fmetres deep, but as England continues
OL,8,Fto face extremely dry conditions, the
OL,9,Fstonework that was left behind after
OL,10,Fthe demolition of Nether Hambleton has
OL,11,Fbeen uncovered by falling water levels.
OL,13,FRainfall across the East Midlands has
OL,14,Fbeen below average for the past five
OL,15,Fconsecutive months, the Environment
OL,16,FAgency (EA) said, with the spring and
OL,17,Fsummer period the driest since 1995
OL,18,Fand July being the driest on record.
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G4/7
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
